<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hisham III of Córdoba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 975–<a href="/years/1036">1036</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hisham III (c. 975–1036) was the last Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, proclaimed in 1026 and installed in the city only in 1029 after years of civil war. His government, run by an unpopular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a>, could not restore order, and in 1031 the notables of Córdoba deposed him and abolished the caliphate. He died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Lleida</a> in 1036, leaving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> divided among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> kingdoms.</p></div>
